# Ghost-Ark code ownership.
#
# The point of this file is narrow: the receipt trust kernel and the mechanisms
# that keep the repository's claims honest should not be modifiable without a
# review from someone who knows why each line is the way it is. Everything else
# is deliberately unowned so that ordinary contribution stays cheap.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern, so the order below is significant.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORGANISATION PRECONDITION — this file has a silent failure mode.
#
# GitHub IGNORES a code owner who does not have write access to the repository,
# and it reports no error when it does so. Under an organisation that means every
# rule below can stop applying while the file still looks correct on disk.
#
# So @Cubits11 must hold write access on PSUCyberSecurityLab/ghost-ark. Verify it
# rather than assume it: open a pull request touching
# packages/enforcement-runtime/src/receipts/ and confirm a reviewer is actually
# requested. If ownership later moves to a lab team, replace the handle with
# @PSUCyberSecurityLab/<team-slug> and re-run the same check — the verification,
# not the edit, is the part that matters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default: no required owner. Ordinary changes do not need a gatekeeper.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Receipt trust kernel — a defect here lets a receipt verify that should not,
# or fails one that should. This is the set measured by experiment E10; keep it
# in sync with tools/experiments/mutationScope.ts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/packages/receipt-schema/src/hashCanonicalization.ts   @Cubits11
/packages/receipt-schema/src/strictJsonAdmission.ts    @Cubits11
/packages/enforcement-runtime/src/receipts/            @Cubits11

# Runtime enforcement, retrieval, and vault paths: fail-closed behavior and
# tenant isolation live here.
/packages/enforcement-runtime/src/runtime/             @Cubits11
/packages/enforcement-runtime/src/retrieval/           @Cubits11
/packages/enforcement-runtime/src/vault/               @Cubits11

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Honesty mechanisms. These are the things that would let the repository
# overclaim if quietly relaxed, so they are owned even though they are tooling.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tools/research/check-forbidden-claims.mjs             @Cubits11
